(Bug #95's nearest working neighbour. The type an untyped declaration fixes
 is the value's own, so a later write of that same type is in order and must
 keep compiling - in every spelling, whichever spelling declared the name.
 A fix that locked too hard would fail here first.)

Set tally to 5.
Set tally to 7.
the tally is 9.
tally is 11.
Print tally.

the label is "first".
Set label to "second".
Print label.

motto is "carry on".
the motto is "carry on regardless".
Print motto.
